<title>USA: TABLE - Fed economic projections for 1997/98.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Fed economic projections for 1997/98.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are the 1997/ 1998 economic projections of Federal Reserve policymakers.</p>
<p>			     (Projections for 1997, Q4 to Q4)</p>
<p>				FED RANGE	FED CENTRAL TENDENCY</p>
<p> Nominal GDP		 5 to 6	     5 to 5-1/2</p>
<p> Real GDP		    3 to 3-1/2	 3 to 3-1/4</p>
<p> CPI			   2 to 2-3/4	 2-1/4 to 2-1/2</p>
<p> Unemployment*	  4-3/4 to 5-1/4	4-3/4 to 5</p>
<p>*Average for fourth quarter</p>
<p>				(Projections for 1998, Q4 to Q4)</p>
<p>				 FED RANGE	FED CENTRAL TENDENCY</p>
<p> Nominal GDP	    4-1/4 to 5-3/4	 4-1/2 to 5</p>
<p> Real GDP		    2 to 3		2 to 2-1/2</p>
<p> CPI			2-1/2 to 3	     2-1/2 to 3</p>
<p> Unemployment*	  4-1/2 to 5-1/4	 4-3/4 to 5</p>
<p>*Average for fourth quarter</p>
</text>
